
class:: ViewCentralModel
summary:: A model for window and view management with persistent state
categories:: gui>views
related:: Classes/ViewCentral, Classes/UserView, Classes/View, Classes/Window

description::
ViewCentralModel is the model class for window classes that centre a view within a variable size window. The class maintains a fixed view size, however view margins and window size can be altered. This functionality can be used to fullscreen a window while keeping a view centered.

The model maintains the state of windows and views, while ViewCentral handles the creation of the gui. A ViewCentralModel intance is passed as an argument into a ViewCentral instance; interaction with the classes should be done via the model.

classmethods::

method:: new
Create a new ViewCentralModel instance.

argument:: dims
An array of two numbers [width, height] specifying the view dimensions, which remain fixed. Defaults to [620, 460] if nil.

argument:: margins
Margins in pixels. Can be a single Integer (applies to all sides), an array of two [horiz, vert], or an array of four [left, top, right, bottom]. Defaults to [20, 20, 20, 20] if nil.

argument:: usrViewBool
Boolean indicating whether to use a UserView (true) or a regular View (false). Defaults to true.


instancemethods::

private:: calcViewDims, calcViewMargSums, cleanMarginsFormat, init

method:: dims
Returns the base dimensions of the view.

method:: viewDims
Returns the dimensions of the inner view area (dims - margins).

method:: marginSums
Returns the sum of margins [horizontal, vertical].

method:: usrViewBool
Returns whether a UserView is being used.

method:: winDims
Get or set the window dimensions.
argument:: dimensions
Window dimensions as an array [width, height].
discussion:: See also the related method link::#-resizeWin::, which has two integers as arguments.

method:: winPos
Get or set the window position.
argument:: position
An array [x, y] specifying the window position in relation to top left.
discussion:: See also the related method link::#-moveWin::, which has two integers as arguments.

method:: winCol
Get or set the window background color.
argument:: color
A Color instance.

method:: viewCol
Get or set the view background color.
argument:: color
A Color instance.

method:: marginCol
Get or set the margin area color.
argument:: color
A Color instance.

method:: margins
Get or set margins for the view layout.

argument:: argMargins
Margins in pixels. Can be a single number (applies to all sides), an array of two [horiz, vert], or an array of four [left, top, right, bottom] values.

method:: winName
Get or set the window name.
argument:: string
A String for the window name.

method:: escKey
Get or set the keycode used to exit fullscreen mode.
argument:: int
The keycode integer. Default is 53 (escape key on MacOS).

method:: restoreCols
Restore all colors to default (monochrome) values.

method:: removeViews
Remove all views from the window without closing it.

method:: shrinkWin
Resize the window to match the original view dimensions.

method:: resizeWin
Resize the window to specified dimensions.
argument:: x
Width in pixels.
argument:: y
Height in pixels.
discussion:: See also method link::#-winDims::, which has an Array argument.

method:: moveWin
Move the window to specified position.
argument:: x
Horizontal position in pixels.
argument:: y
Vertical position in pixels.
discussion:: See also method link::#-winPos::, which has an Array argument.

method:: endFullScreen
Exit fullscreen mode. Usually performed using the escKey.

method:: screenHeight
Get the screenHeight

method:: fullScreen
Enter fullscreen mode.

method:: front
Bring the window to front.

method:: close
Close the window.


examples::

code::
// Create model and view
m = ViewCentralModel.new([300, 600], 50!4);
v = ViewCentral.new(Window().front, m);

// Demonstrate fullscreen and escape key handling
// press escape key (Apple MPP) to end fullScreen
m.escKey // 53
m.fullScreen
m.escKey_(12) // 'q' - see "KeyState".help
m.fullScreen

// Get information about the window and views

m.dims // [300, 600]
m.margins // [50, 50, 50, 50]
m.marginSums // [100, 100]

// Modify margins and dimensions
m.margins_([100, 50])
m.margins_(19)
m.margins_(0) // the margins disapear
m.resizeWin(500, 620)
m.moveWin(0, 0);
m.shrinkWin; // same as resizeWin(*m.dims);


// Change colors
m.resizeWin(360, 660)// reveals window background
m.margins_(30) // reveals margins
m.viewCol_(Color.green);
m.winCol_(Color.yellow);
m.marginCol_(Color.red);

// Set window name
m.winName_("My Colorfuel Window")

// Close the window
m.close;

// Demonstrate persistent layout with a new window
(
// Create model with specific settings
m = ViewCentralModel.new([300, 300], 75!4);
v = ViewCentral.new(Window().front, m);

// Configure appearance
m.resizeWin(400, 400);
m.moveWin(0, 0);
m.viewCol_(Color.green);
m.winCol_(Color.yellow);
m.marginCol_(Color.red);
)

// Close the window
m.close;

// Remake window - layout is preserved in model
v = ViewCentral.new(nil, m);

m.removeViews // removes green view with red margin

// Remake views using existing window
v = ViewCentral.new(v.win, m);
m.restoreCols // monochrome
m.close;
::


